# Max Showdown Trivia — Project Reference

## Project Summary

Real-time web-based trivia platform for live events. Minimum 300 concurrent players, sub-200ms latency. Four interfaces:
- **Host Control Panel** (desktop web) — quiz master command centre
- **Player Mobile Interface** (responsive mobile web) — no native app
- **Venue Display Screen** (projected/TV) — 16:9 widescreen
- **Admin Panel** (web) — content management, quiz builder, session config

Purpose: Replace third-party trivia software; host has full control over format, branding, and live show experience.

---

## User Types

| Type | Device | Role |
|------|--------|------|
| **Players/Teams** | Smartphone | Join via QR, enter PIN + team name, answer questions. Team-based (solo = team of one). One device per team. |
| **Host/Quiz Master** | Desktop/laptop | Control game flow, timers, reveal, leaderboard, manual team management. Uses Admin for prep. |
| **Venue Audience** | Passive | View projected screen only. All audio via venue sound system. |
| **Admin** | Desktop | Create quizzes, question bank, upload MP3/MP4, configure sessions, generate PINs/QR codes. Same person as Host (Max). |

---

## Technology Stack (JavaScript Only)

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Frontend | Next.js (React), Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion |
| Backend | Node.js, Express or Fastify |
| Real-time | Socket.io |
| Database | MySQL + Sequelize |
| Cache | Redis |
| 3D Mini-games | Three.js or Babylon.js |
| Validation | Zod |
| Media Storage | S3/R2 or Supabase Storage |
| QR Generation | qrcode (npm) |

No C#, no Unity, no PostgreSQL, no Prisma.

---

## Architecture (300+ Concurrent Users)

- Load balancer → Next.js (static) → Game server (Socket.io)
- One game server per session; sticky sessions for WebSocket affinity
- Redis: live game state, lobby, scores, session presence
- MySQL: quizzes, questions, sessions, teams (persistent)
- Socket.io Redis adapter if multiple game server instances
- Connection pool: MySQL 20–50 per server; keep Redis connection minimal

---

## Host Control Panel (Web — Desktop/Laptop)

**Game Session Dashboard:** Question X/Total, full question text, round name/type, connected teams count, response count for current question, live leaderboard (always visible before venue), points per question.

**Game Controls:** Start Timer (T), Pause Timer (P), Reveal Answer (button), Next Question (Space), Show Leaderboard (S). Timer sound plays (muted during Music rounds).

**Music Round Controls:** Play/pause for MP3; audio via host laptop → venue sound. On Next: timer + MP3 + options appear simultaneously. No timer sound during Music. Video (MP4): play/pause on venue screen.

**Mini-Game Launcher:** Launch Horse Race or Card Shuffle anytime. Displays on venue; players interact via mobile.

**Manual Team Management:** Add team (with custom score), remove team, edit any team's score. Use case: re-add reconnected team with previous score.

---

## Player Mobile Interface (Responsive Web)

**Session Join:** Scan QR → server URL. Enter session PIN + team name. Persistent QR on every slide for late join.

**Lobby:** Waiting screen until host starts. Team name displayed; "connected and waiting" confirmation.

**Question & Answer:** Question text, 2–6 answer options as tappable cards. First answer final (locked). One submission per team per question. Countdown visible on phone. Video plays on venue only; players see text + options.

**Answer Reveal:** Green (correct) / red (incorrect) feedback; points gained/lost shown.

**Wager Rounds:** Standard — select 0–50 pts before question. Final — select 0–100% of total score. Then question displays, answer as normal.

**Elimination:** Wrong answer → "Unfortunately, you've been knocked out until the end of the round." Rejoin next round.

**Majority Rules:** Vote; majority +50, minority −50.

**3D Mini-Games:** Horse Race — bet on horse. Card Shuffle — pick target card (e.g. Queen) after shuffle.

**Reconnection:** Same PIN + team name; score preserved. If lost, host manually re-adds with previous score.

**No audio on player devices.**

---

## Venue Display Screen (Web — Projected/TV)

16:9 layout. View-only, host-controlled. **Welcome Screen** (branded, animated logo). **Team Registration Grid** (numbered slots, green + tick when team joins). **Round Header.** **Round Intro Slide.** **Question Display** (text, options, optional video). **Countdown Timer.** **Live Response Counter.** **Answer Reveal** (correct highlighted). **Leaderboard Display.** **QR Code** (persistent on every slide). **Mini-Game Display.** **Break Timer** (e.g. 6 min). **Points Display.** **Auto-Reveal** when all teams answer.

---

## Admin Panel (Web)

**Quiz Builder:** Create quizzes, define rounds, order, types. **Question Bank:** Reusable questions, categorise, search, 2–6 options per question. **MP3 Upload:** For Music rounds. **MP4 Upload:** For video questions (observation, music videos). **Session Configuration:** Max teams, timer durations, scoring rules per quiz, round types. **Preview** full quiz flow before live. **Session Creation:** Generate unique PIN, QR code.

---

## Game Flow Sequence

Lobby → Round Intro → Question → Timer starts + options appear (+ MP3 if Music) → Answer Reveal → Score Update → Next Question → Round End → Leaderboard → Next Round → … → Final Wager → Final Results.

Host controls all transitions. **Auto-reveal:** if all teams answer before timer, reveal immediately. No other auto-advance.

---

## Game State Machine

**Global states:** LOBBY | ROUND_INTRO | QUESTION | SCOREBOARD | BREAK | MINI_GAME | FINAL_WAGER | FINAL_RESULTS

**Question sub-states:** WAITING → ACTIVE (timer running, accepting) → REVEALED. All-teams-answered → AUTO_REVEAL_TRIGGERED.

Host can enter BREAK anytime; during break launch MINI_GAME (Horse Race or Card Shuffle).

---

## Break + Mini-Games Flow

1. Host "Start Break" → Venue shows break timer (e.g. 6 min)
2. Host "Launch Horse Race" or "Launch Card Shuffle" during break
3. Teams play via mobile; no trivia score impact
4. Host can launch other mini-game or "End Break"
5. Timer expires or host ends → resume trivia

---

## Round Types (7 Total)

1. **Multiple Choice** — +10 / −2
2. **Wager** (standard) — +wager / −wager (0–50 pts)
3. **Music** — +10 / −2; MP3 plays; no timer sound
4. **Elimination** — incremental 10–120 pts; knockout (see below)
5. **Majority Rules** — majority +50, minority −50
6. **Final Multiple Choice** — +10 / −2
7. **Final Wager** — +wager / −wager (0–100% of score)

---

## Knockout (Elimination Round)

12 questions. Points: 10, 20, 30 … 120. Wrong → knocked out for remainder of round. **All-teams-wrong rule:** if all remaining teams wrong on same question → no elimination; all lose points, all continue. Elimination only when some correct, some wrong. Eliminated teams rejoin next round. Pop-up: "Unfortunately, you've been knocked out until the end of the round."

